A_653 - Continuing from the previous element and wanting to imagine a world where animals are not mutilated (of the wings or genitals, to prevent them from reproducing) there is an important consideration to make: in certain cases they would obviously die either from hunger or because they were hit or crushed by a vehicle, so if we want to move in a direction where animals are free to roam and are not mutilated it would be extremely important for the profession of gravedigger to be accepted and respected, because obviously the carcasses of dead animals would absolutely have to be buried.